  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Horticulture project in Kumasi</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Together with partners, the Netherlands aims to contribute to a vibrant horticulture sector in Ghana.One of the pathways of change is working on skills development of youth (students) in agriculture. This is done together with knowledge institutes in Ghana and in the Netherlands, and with the private sector.At the end of this project, the following results will be achieved:1.	Additional trainees and lead farmers are trained in Kumasi;2.	Implement a framework of greenhouse technology to the Kwadaso Agricultural College (KAC);3.	Better understanding of the training needs in: Volta region (Ohawu Agricultural College), Northern region (Damango Agricultural College), Ashanti region (Ejura Agricultural College), Bono Ahafo region (Wenchi Agricultural College);4.	Lead farmers in the Volta Region are supported for two growing seasons;5.	Better understanding of a long-term project/scale with other partners.</narrative>
  </description>
